              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Marathi for inspiration, then the Marathi for to bother."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: अट",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "अट — aṭ — \"a condition (stipulation)\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "करारात एक महत्त्वाची अट होती. karārāt ek mahattvācī aṭ hotī. There was an important condition in the contract."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Feminine. Plural: अटी, aṭī."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "अटीवर, on condition: एका अटीवर हो म्हणणे, to say yes on one condition."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "अट (aṭ) is usually traced to the root aṭṭ-, \"obstruct, stop\", under which CDIAL lists Marathi aṭ, \"obstruction\" (CDIAL 179): a condition holds a thing back."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for saying what happens if."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
