            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Marathi for to bother, then the Marathi for a condition."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: अपवाद",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "अपवाद — apvād — \"an exception\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "हा नियम सगळ्यांना लागू आहे, कोणीही अपवाद नाही. hā niyam sagaḷyānnā lāgū āhe, koṇīhī apvād nāhī. This rule applies to everyone; nobody is an exception."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Masculine."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "अपवादाने, as an exception; X चा अपवाद (apvād), the exception to X."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "अपवाद (apvād) is a tatsama, taken from Sanskrit apavāda, \"evil speaking\", which grammarians also used for a special rule that sets a general one aside, an exception (Monier-Williams). The same head gave the inherited Marathi avāī, \"rumour\" (CDIAL 456)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
